  "system": {
    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Rebellion_Era_Campaign_Guide\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Rebellion Era Campaign Guide\">Star Wars Saga Edition Rebellion Era Campaign Guide</a></i> </p><p>Designed for use with <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Zero-Gravity_Stormtrooper_Armor\" title=\"Zero-Gravity Stormtrooper Armor\">Zero-Gravity Stormtrooper Armor</a>, Miniature Proton Torpedoes can rip through Starship hulls. The launcher mounts into the Zero-Gravity Stormtrooper Armor's left gauntlet, but enterprising Rebel engineers have adapted the Weapon as a shoulder-mounted launcher. </p><p>After launching a Miniature Proton Torpedo, the wielder must spend a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Standard_Action\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Standard Action\">Standard Action</a> to reset the launcher, which holds 4 torpedoes. </p><p>When you make an&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Area_Attack\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Area Attack\">Area Attack</a>&nbsp;with a Miniature Proton Torpedo Launcher, you make a single attack roll and compare the result to the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Reflex_Defense\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Reflex Defense\">Reflex Defense</a>&nbsp;of every target in the Weapon's 2-Square&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Burst\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Burst\">Burst</a>&nbsp;radius. Creatures you hit take full damage, and creatures you miss take half damage. A target with the&nbsp;<b><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Evasion\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Evasion\">Evasion</a></b>&nbsp;Talent takes half damage from a successful attack, and no damage if the attack misses. </p><p>Alternatively, the Weapon can be fired at a single target, acting as a focused weapon designed to take out Starfighters and Ground Vehicles. As a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Swift_Action\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Swift Action\">Swift Action</a>, you can set the Miniature Proton Torpedo Launcher to single-target mode. In this mode, the weapon no longer functions as an <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Area_Attack\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Area Attack\">Area Attack</a> Weapon, deals 6d10x2 damage, and applies a -10 penalty on attack rolls against targets smaller than Huge size. </p><p>Replacement Miniature Proton Torpedoes weigh 5 kg and cost 200 credits each. </p><p><b>Special:</b>&nbsp;This is an&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Area_Attack\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Area Attack\">Area Attack</a>&nbsp;Weapon. </p>",
